    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, which is the only test class) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily create-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: once 100 or more owners have already been registered on the current day, a create is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the existing per-city capacity guard as the template, I added:\n\n- **`EnsureDailyLimit.java`** \u2014 a guard step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (matching the date a new owner defaults to via `DefaultRegistrationDate`), throwing when the count reaches `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100). It injects only `OwnerRepository` \u2014 the check needs nothing from the request.\n- **`DailyLimitReachedException.java`** \u2014 a checked escalation carrying the day, mirroring `CityAtCapacityException`.\n- **`DailyLimitReachedExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 429 with a `ProblemDetail` built by the shared `ProblemDetails` helper.\n- **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n- Wired **`ensureDailyLimit`** into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureCityCapacity` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nEach piece has a single responsibility and reuses the existing escalation/`ProblemDetails` infrastructure rather than duplicating it.",
